{"id": "EUVD-2026-108765", "enisaUuid": "4d0f7019-948c-3b73-b44d-428119fb7682", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: exar: initialize the ID before registering its cleanup\n\ndevm_add_action_or_reset() invokes the cleanup action immediately when\nregistering the action fails.  gpio_exar_probe() currently stores the\nallocated ID in exar_gpio only after registering the action, so that\nfailure makes exar_devm_ida_free() release ID 0.  If the allocated ID is\nnonzero, this leaks that ID and can free ID 0 belonging to another device.\n\nStore the ID before registering the cleanup action so both the immediate\nfailure path and normal device teardown release the correct allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf3d841ef12fcbec4458e2750956b738b043a226", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b78c114600ae3df90c083c72c290437b068577c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01318927a9055136c207399eeb36ce07becac179", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7ec4dbd2a073dd53b6349be1c586fe8580dd6b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d69e74034b208588636ecc177e0dd43a7696af3"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98971"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f85f747-af45-31c9-b9c6-28ca4f36d0f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5300ebb695fa0672589ab191062392f686fca75d <bf3d841ef12fcbec4458e2750956b738b043a226"}, {"id": "261f9c95-f0cd-381d-b6d8-96e3c43b09d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5300ebb695fa0672589ab191062392f686fca75d <b78c114600ae3df90c083c72c290437b068577c8"}, {"id": "428a0bf7-ddf7-3d57-8787-88ff7dfe12d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5300ebb695fa0672589ab191062392f686fca75d <4d69e74034b208588636ecc177e0dd43a7696af3"}, {"id": "429f1887-9b4e-328e-be93-95c693db1960", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5300ebb695fa0672589ab191062392f686fca75d <f7ec4dbd2a073dd53b6349be1c586fe8580dd6b2"}, {"id": "53f264eb-6207-362c-b4ca-c4f98fd5b96d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "54280167-3f29-3d58-92b3-eea651751df7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "71aca0ed-7ae0-37bf-808e-eddc2984f6c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "771db4fd-95e9-343a-81b5-2a59d2f7111c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5300ebb695fa0672589ab191062392f686fca75d <01318927a9055136c207399eeb36ce07becac179"}, {"id": "846211fd-e6ce-31a4-8398-d05495b411e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "aef8cf9b-db0e-3bc0-a02f-dcd1d092dc09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e67e5e96-da0b-3e49-94e8-b166fd8873e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "f7eaf779-8291-33ab-be34-d2dc7835dc22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "29ac1864-fb3a-334d-ac87-ea8390f7bdec", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}